WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.801
(protester leader speaking
in foreign language)

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.331
(protesters speaking in foreign language)

00:00:03.331 --> 00:00:04.164
(protester leader speaking
in foreign language)

00:00:04.164 --> 00:00:04.997
- [Narrator] Imagine if your bank accounts

00:00:04.997 --> 00:00:06.503
were frozen without warning.

00:00:06.503 --> 00:00:09.840
(protesters speaking in foreign language)

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.280
Or you've been paying for an apartment

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.660
that hasn't been built.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.040
That's happening in China

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.190
where economic woes have
pushed people to the streets,

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.130
and some people online, like
homeowners who are threatening

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.600
to stop paying their mortgages

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.580
until developers clear construction delays

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.830
and hand over the homes they bought.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.930
China's GDP growth was close to zero

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.010
during the second quarter

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.070
amid COVID lockdowns
and supply chain issues.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.990
These protests highlight specific troubles

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:35.610
and parts of China's economy.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.740
So here's what's happening
and how the authorities

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.733
are trying to keep things under control.

00:00:39.733 --> 00:00:41.916
(protesters clamoring)

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:44.490
(apprehensive music)

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:46.920
In China, there's been no
room for political protests

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.630
to challenge the leadership.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.070
Just look at Beijing's suppression

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.325
of Hong Kong's pro-democracy
movement since 2019.

00:00:53.325 --> 00:00:54.810
(protesters speaking in foreign language)

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.880
But the protests this
summer are different.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.410
- This shows the recent
pattern mass protest in China

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:05.430
'cause people have
immediate issues to address

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:08.310
that really affect themselves directly.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.320
- [Narrator] Tai Zixue
is an associate professor

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.500
who's been studying social
activism in China for 20 years.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.770
He says protestors can't target
the ruling communist party

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:18.150
if they want to be heard.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:19.410
- If you have political demands,

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.240
there's no room for negotiation

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.850
but the scenarios we
have seen are different.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.070
They're not political; they're economic

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.650
or financial interest driven.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:29.483
- [Narrator] One major issue

00:01:29.483 --> 00:01:31.650
has been the country's real estate sector.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:35.040
Collectively, urban Chinese
have nearly 78% of their wealth

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.960
tied up in residential property.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.820
And many have yet to see their new homes

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.770
because developers don't have enough money

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.590
to finish building
apartments they've pre-sold.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.060
To get a sense of how homeowners

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.740
have been left waiting in limbo,

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:48.390
take a look at this chart.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.640
The blue line shows the
number of housing projects

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.190
that started construction in 2021.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:55.050
The red line is the number of projects

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.490
that have been completed.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.080
There are few reasons for this.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.730
First, the government's strict limits

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.350
on property developers' leverage

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.930
cause some of them to
default on their debt.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.870
Add on top of that, the slowing
economy and COVID lockdowns

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:08.730
that triggered a drop in home sales

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:12.120
which fell nearly 40% in
July compared to last year.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.520
As a result, many developers
have had less cash

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.200
to fund construction.
(light music)

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.210
So frustrated fires of unfinished homes

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:20.250
have joined a movement
that's been gathering steam

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.960
on Chinese social media.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.510
These are hundreds of joint
letters issued by homeowners

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.330
for more than 100 cities
across the country.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:28.650
They've been circulating online

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.050
and all of them share a similar message

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.730
that they'll stop their mortgage payments

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:36.090
until developers finish and
hand over the apartments.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:38.130
The mortgage revolt left
authority scrambling

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:41.490
to reassure home buyers that
projects will be completed.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.640
Some local governments rolled
out tax rebates, cash rewards,

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.460
and lower down payments to
boost their property markets.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:50.160
- It's tradition, Chinese protests.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:54.348
You have to make a very
loud voice to get heard.

00:02:54.348 --> 00:02:56.220
(protesters speaking in foreign language)

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.053
- [Narrator] Another problem

00:02:57.053 --> 00:02:58.280
that's triggered loud complaints, thanks.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.710
In the city of Zhengzhou,
protestors vented their anger

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.410
at rural lenders for
freezing their accounts.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.450
This comes amid a government investigation

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.570
into financial misconduct by
a private investment group.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:12.210
- Their immediate deal is
to get their money back.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:15.243
They're not asking
anything more than that.

00:03:16.414 --> 00:03:19.664
(protesters clamoring)

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:21.563
- [Narrator] Chaos erupted

00:03:21.563 --> 00:03:23.970
when a group of unidentified
men in white T-shirts

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.410
ramped into the crowd.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.810
The Wall Street Journal couldn't
determine their identity

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.730
and neither the bank
nor the local government

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.680
responded to request for comment.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.960
The incident went viral
on Chinese social media

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.150
and got the attention of the authorities.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.860
That's when local officials stepped in

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.870
and made concessions to
appease demonstrators

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:42.090
with two rounds of
repayments to depositors.

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.650
- They are giving indications

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:45.690
that the government is
working with those issues.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.048
That's the typical strategy.

00:03:48.048 --> 00:03:49.050
(bright music)

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:49.890
- [Narrator] For China's leaders,

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.860
maintaining stability is
a top economic priority.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.660
So to stop the protest from growing,

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:57.240
the country's top policy-making
body said it would work

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.850
to resolve problems in
the rural banking system.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:02.550
And it told local governments
to take direct responsibility

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.080
for delivering unfinished homes

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.300
and supporting demand for housing.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.780
- So without finding ways
to keep the economy going,

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:11.310
more problems will show up.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.800
This may be the opportunity
for them to figure out,

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:16.080
okay, what's the best way to move forward.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.760
And also to find ways

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.510
into the national economic
policy to solve those issues.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:22.920
- [Narrator] Stability is also the back

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.930
to our president Xi
Jinping needs as he tries

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:28.294
to secure a precedent-breaking
third term in a few months.

00:04:28.294 --> 00:04:31.377
(apprehensive music)

